{
  "info": {
    "name": "CleanCom API",
    "description": "Flujo completo del API de CleanCom (semana 1): sesión, configuración de Operación, catálogos y usuarios.\n\nAntes de correr:\n1. Variables de la colección: `baseUrl` (por defecto http://localhost:5111), `userName` y `password` de un usuario de Administración.\n2. Si el usuario todavía debe cambiar su contraseña inicial, llena `newPassword`; el paso 0.2 la cambia y actualiza `password`. Si no, el 0.2 se salta solo.\n3. Corre en orden (uno por uno o con el Runner). Los scripts guardan tokens e IDs.\n\nLos pasos marcados (escribe) crean o cambian datos. Úsala contra `cleancom_dev`, nunca contra producción. Cada corrida usa un suffix distinto, así que se puede repetir sin choques de códigos.\n\nNo guardes contraseñas reales en este archivo: llénalas en tu Postman (valor actual) o en un environment local.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:5111" },
    { "key": "userName", "value": "admin" },
    { "key": "password", "value": "" },
    { "key": "newPassword", "value": "" },
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "refreshToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "mustChange", "value": "" },
    { "key": "suffix", "value": "" },
    { "key": "rutaId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "zonaNucleoId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "zonaExtId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "lugarId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "reasonId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "nonWorkingDayId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "nonWorkingDate", "value": "" },
    { "key": "coverageId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "userId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "operadorId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "roleId", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0 · Sesión",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "0.1 · Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 sesión', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const s = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', s.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', s.refreshToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('mustChange', String(s.user.mustChangePassword));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('suffix', Date.now().toString().slice(-6));",
                  "if (s.user.mustChangePassword) { console.log('El usuario debe cambiar su contraseña: corre 0.2 con newPassword.'); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"userName\": \"{{userName}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] },
            "description": "Acepta usuario o correo. 401 con credenciales incorrectas; 5 intentos fallidos bloquean la cuenta 15 minutos."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "0.2 · Cambiar contraseña (solo si debe cambiarla)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.collectionVariables.get('mustChange') !== 'true') {",
                  "  console.log('0.2 se salta: el usuario ya cambió su contraseña.');",
                  "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 sesión nueva', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const s = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', s.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', s.refreshToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('mustChange', 'false');",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('password', pm.collectionVariables.get('newPassword'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"currentPassword\": \"{{password}}\",\n  \"newPassword\": \"{{newPassword}}\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/cambiar-contrasena", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "cambiar-contrasena"] },
            "description": "Mínimo 8 caracteres y distinta de la actual. Regresa una sesión nueva con el token completo y cierra las demás sesiones."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "0.3 · ¿Quién soy?",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('ya no debe cambiar contraseña', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().mustChangePassword).to.be.false);",
                  "pm.test('puede editar Operación y Usuarios', () => {",
                  "  const p = pm.response.json().permissions;",
                  "  pm.expect(p).to.include('operacion:edit');",
                  "  pm.expect(p).to.include('usuarios:edit');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/yo", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "yo"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "0.4 · Renovar sesión",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 tokens nuevos', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const anterior = pm.collectionVariables.get('refreshToken');",
                  "const s = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('el token de renovación cambia', () => pm.expect(s.refreshToken).to.not.eql(anterior));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', s.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', s.refreshToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/renovar", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "renovar"] },
            "description": "Cada token de renovación sirve una vez. Reusar uno ya usado cierra todas las sesiones del usuario."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1 · Configuración",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1.1 · Valores vigentes",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const lista = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('26 claves', () => pm.expect(lista.length).to.eql(26));",
                  "pm.test('existe el corte del mismo día', () => pm.expect(lista.map(c => c.key)).to.include('Agenda.CorteMismoDia'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/configuracion", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["configuracion"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1.2 · Cambiar un valor (escribe)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 renglón del historial', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('valor normalizado', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().value).to.eql('10'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"key\": \"Ruta.MetaRecolecciones\",\n  \"value\": \"10\",\n  \"effectiveFrom\": null,\n  \"note\": \"Prueba Postman (mismo valor)\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/configuracion", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["configuracion"] },
            "description": "Pone el mismo valor que ya tiene para no alterar la operación; solo agrega un renglón al historial. Con `effectiveFrom` futuro el cambio queda programado; en el pasado responde 400."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1.3 · Clave inexistente → 400",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('400 validación', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('mensaje en español', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().errors.Key[0]).to.include('no existe'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"key\": \"Agenda.NoExiste\",\n  \"value\": \"13:00\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/configuracion", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["configuracion"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1.4 · Historial de una clave",
          "event": [
            { "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"] } }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/configuracion/historial?key=Ruta.MetaRecolecciones",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["configuracion", "historial"],
              "query": [{ "key": "key", "value": "Ruta.MetaRecolecciones" }]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2 · Catálogos",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "2.1 · Crear ruta (escribe)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 creada', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('rutaId', pm.response.json().id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"code\": \"P{{suffix}}\",\n  \"name\": \"Ruta de prueba {{suffix}}\",\n  \"color\": \"#1E88E5\",\n  \"cupoParadas\": 16,\n  \"recoleccionGoal\": null,\n  \"maxReturnTime\": null,\n  \"maxReturnTimeSaturday\": \"14:30:00\",\n  \"active\": true\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rutas", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["rutas"] },
            "description": "Código en mayúsculas sin espacios y color #RRGGBB. Cupo, meta y horas de regreso vacíos toman el valor general de Configuración."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.2 · Ruta repetida → 409",
          "event": [
            { "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('409 ya existe', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));"] } }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"code\": \"P{{suffix}}\",\n  \"name\": \"Otra\",\n  \"color\": \"#000000\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rutas", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["rutas"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.3 · Listar rutas",
          "event": [
            { "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"] } }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rutas", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["rutas"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.4 · Crear zona núcleo (escribe)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 creada', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('zonaNucleoId', pm.response.json().id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"code\": \"Z{{suffix}}\",\n  \"rutaId\": {{rutaId}},\n  \"zonaNucleoId\": null,\n  \"polygon\": [\n    { \"lat\": 19.3712, \"lng\": -99.2051 },\n    { \"lat\": 19.3655, \"lng\": -99.1987 },\n    { \"lat\": 19.3598, \"lng\": -99.2063 }\n  ],\n  \"active\": true\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/zonas", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["zonas"] },
            "description": "El polígono va en latitud y longitud, mínimo 3 vértices; se cierra solo."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.5 · Días de visita del núcleo (escribe)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('lunes y jueves', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().visitDays).to.eql(['Monday', 'Thursday']));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"days\": [\"Monday\", \"Thursday\"]\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/zonas/{{zonaNucleoId}}/dias", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["zonas", "{{zonaNucleoId}}", "dias"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.6 · Crear zona EXT (escribe)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 creada', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const z = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('zonaExtId', z.id);",
                  "pm.test('sin días propios', () => pm.expect(z.visitDays).to.eql([]));",
                  "pm.test('hereda los días del núcleo', () => pm.expect(z.effectiveVisitDays).to.eql(['Monday', 'Thursday']));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"code\": \"Z{{suffix}}EXT\",\n  \"rutaId\": {{rutaId}},\n  \"zonaNucleoId\": {{zonaNucleoId}},\n  \"polygon\": [],\n  \"active\": true\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/zonas", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["zonas"] },
            "description": "Regla de negocio: una zona EXT sigue los días de visita de su zona núcleo."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.7 · Días de una zona EXT → 400",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('400 regla de negocio', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('explica que siga al núcleo', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().detail).to.include('núcleo'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"days\": [\"Friday\"]\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/zonas/{{zonaExtId}}/dias", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["zonas", "{{zonaExtId}}", "dias"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.8 · Zonas de la ruta",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('núcleo y EXT', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().length).to.eql(2));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/zonas?rutaId={{rutaId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["zonas"],
              "query": [{ "key": "rutaId", "value": "{{rutaId}}" }, { "key": "includeInactive", "value": "false", "disabled": true }]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.9 · Lugares",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('está la base Leones', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().map(l => l.name)).to.include('Leones'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/lugares", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["lugares"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.10 · Crear lugar (escribe)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 creado', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('lugarId', pm.response.json().id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Tienda de prueba {{suffix}}\",\n  \"type\": \"Tienda\",\n  \"address\": \"Av. Revolución 1500, Guadalupe Inn, Álvaro Obregón\",\n  \"lat\": 19.3589,\n  \"lng\": -99.1890,\n  \"openingHours\": \"L-V 9:00-19:00\",\n  \"active\": true\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/lugares", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["lugares"] },
